is move clears the \'trash\' single and forces opponents to spend an Ace or the final 2 if they wish to regain the lead. Holding the King risks getting stuck with it later, while playing a 2 is unnecessary force, and playing an Ace breaks a strong pair.\n\nReason: Playing the King clears the only single card in the hand, leaving a highly structured hand of pairs and a triplet of 2s. It effectively challenges the opponents\' high cards while maintaining board control with the 2s.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣K"]}'}
